# Reproducible Phase-9 production outputs are local build products. The raw
# and canonical JSONL files exceed GitHub's per-file limit; commit their
# versioned builders/contracts, not regenerated bulk data.
artifacts/data/synthetic/final/
artifacts/data/synthetic/cohorts/final/
artifacts/data/synthetic/timelines/final/
artifacts/data/synthetic/features/final/
artifacts/data/synthetic/pre_split/final/
artifacts/data/synthetic/phase10/final/
artifacts/test-results/

# Same rationale for the Performance-V2 Phase-3 fresh test cohort's raw/
# cohort/timeline/features/pre_split pipeline outputs: large, deterministic
# rebuilds. The small spec/audit/split/freeze artifacts that hash-bind them
# (artifacts/performance_v2/phase3/fresh_test_cohort_*.json, fresh_test_split_*,
# artifacts/performance_v2/governance/v2_fresh_test_*.json) remain tracked.
artifacts/performance_v2/phase3/fresh_test_cohort/

# Read-only historical/reference repository; never vendor as an embedded Git repo.
Heart-Failure-Recovery-and-Deterioration-Trajectory-Prediction/

# Frontend (SvelteKit): dependencies and build output are regenerated via
# `npm install` / `npm run build`, never committed.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.svelte-kit/
frontend/build/
frontend/.vercel/
frontend/.vite/

# Playwright: saved auth state (a live session token) and run artifacts.
frontend/tests/e2e/.auth/
frontend/playwright-report/
frontend/test-results/

# Kokoro narration microservice: isolated Python 3.12 venv (kokoro-onnx needs
# a newer onnxruntime than the project's pinned Python 3.9) and its
# downloaded model weights. Regenerate with the commands in RUNBOOK.md; never
# commit a ~340MB binary pair or a second interpreter's site-packages.
.venv-tts/
models/kokoro/*.onnx
models/kokoro/*.bin

# Health-record report uploads (local object-storage backend): user-supplied
# files, synthetic/demo-only by policy, never committed. See
# src/serving/v2/report_storage.py and docs/product_v2/HEALTH_RECORD_ARCHITECTURE.md.
runtime/uploads/
